{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (NURSE): Come on in and sit yourself down. I'll grab the blood pressure before the doctor, the machine takes a minute.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Grand, sure. I nearly didn't bother coming at all. It's hardly anything.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (NURSE): One thirty eight over eighty six, and the pulse is seventy two. The chart here has you down for rampiril ten milligrams.",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (PATIENT): Ah no. It's five. Five milligrams. They dropped the ten last year, or whenever it was.",
  "[SEG0005] person_1 (NURSE): I'll flag that for him so. My own sister, she lives down in Galway, she had a breast lump last spring. She's only thirty two and it was a cyst in the end.",
  "[SEG0006] person_3 (DOCTOR): Sorry, err, I'm with you now. This yoke keeps freezing on me. What was it brought you in?",
  "[SEG0007] person_2 (PATIENT): It's only a wee lump. Left breast. I found it in the shower and it's not sore, so I doubt it's much.",
  "[SEG0008] person_3 (DOCTOR): Sorry, say that again? The screen just jumped.",
  "[SEG0009] person_2 (PATIENT): A lump, left side. Couple of weeks back, in the shower. No pain in it. I wouldn't be losing sleep.",
  "[SEG0010] person_3 (DOCTOR): Right. Any discharge out of the nipple?",
  "[SEG0011] person_2 (PATIENT): No. Nothing at all. I'd have seen it.",
  "[SEG0012] person_3 (DOCTOR): Any dimpling of the skin, or a rash on that breast?",
  "[SEG0013] person_2 (PATIENT): No. Skin's grand. It's just that small lump and even that's tiny.",
  "[SEG0014] person_3 (DOCTOR): And your mam, or sisters, any breast cancer in the family?",
  "[SEG0015] person_2 (PATIENT): My mother, yeah. Breast cancer. She was fifty five. She's grand this long while, it was years ago.",
  "[SEG0016] person_3 (DOCTOR): Fifty five. Uh, hold on, it wants the password again. Were you caught in that rain on the way over?",
  "[SEG0017] person_2 (PATIENT): Desperate. The M50 was stopped dead and the hurling was on the radio, Limerick, and I only heard bits of it. My brother was texting the whole time, delighted.",
  "[SEG0018] person_3 (DOCTOR): Mm. They were very handy on Sunday. I only caught the second half myself. That referee though.",
  "[SEG0019] person_2 (PATIENT): Don't start me. We were still at it over the dinner, arguing the frees. Pure nonsense. Anyway.",
  "[SEG0020] person_3 (DOCTOR): Right so. I'll have a feel of it if you're ok with that.",
  "[SEG0021] person_2 (PATIENT): Fire ahead. You'll see it's nothing.",
  "[SEG0022] person_3 (DOCTOR): There's a small firm lump in the upper outer left breast, about two centimetres, and it moves under the finger. Skin's not pulled in. No glands in the armpit, and the right breast is clear.",
  "[SEG0023] person_2 (PATIENT): Tiny, like I said.",
  "[SEG0024] person_3 (DOCTOR): Often enough a lump like that is the breast tissue thickening where the hormones act on the little ducts, and they get a bit clogged. That's the body doing its ordinary work. It still has to be checked.",
  "[SEG0025] person_2 (PATIENT): So you're saying it's nothing.",
  "[SEG0026] person_3 (DOCTOR): I'm not. I can't rule out something more serious, painless or not. I'm referring you urgently to the breast clinic.",
  "[SEG0027] person_3 (DOCTOR): They'll see you within two weeks, and they'll do the mammogram and the ultrasound up there. If the skin starts dimpling or you see blood from the nipple, don't sit on it, ring us the same day.",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (PATIENT): Two weeks is grand. Am I needing tablets?",
  "[SEG0029] person_3 (DOCTOR): No tablets from me. Any reactions to medicines before? A rash, swelling, anything like that?",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (PATIENT): Umm. Maybe. Years back I came out in a rash. Could've been the antibiotic or the painkiller, nobody told me which.",
  "[SEG0031] person_3 (DOCTOR): Sorry, once more? It flashed up a warning there.",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (PATIENT): A rash. I never found out if it was the antibiotic or the painkiller. That's the height of it.",
  "[SEG0033] person_1 (NURSE): I'll send the referral through from the desk now so you're not waiting. Mind that rain on the way home."
 ],
